speechtext:
The leader of the Opposition asked how the Bankruptcy Act would affect this section. Section 2, subsection (k), of that Act says:
"Corporation" includes any company incorporated or authorized to carry on business by or under an Act of the Parliament of Canada or of any of the provinces of Canada, and any incorporated company, wheresoever incorporated, which has an office in or carries on business within Canada, but does not include bundling societies having a capital stock, nor incorporated banks, savings banks, insurance companies, trust companies, loan companies or railway companies;
So that railway companies are not excepted.
